# No trailing slash, deliberately.
#
# `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY called node_modules and nothing else. A
# symlink called node_modules — which is what a linked local dependency is, and
# what several package managers create — is not a directory, so the pattern
# misses it and the link gets committed. That has happened on a sibling module
# once already: a symlink pointing at its own parent went into a commit, and
# every checkout afterwards failed with ELOOP.
node_modules

# The build. Nothing serves it — `run.sh` runs Vite — and a checked-in copy is a
# second answer to "what does this page say", which disagrees with the first the
# moment somebody edits `src/`.
dist

# This app's own store: the suites somebody configured and the runs recorded
# against a reference. Both are facts about THIS MACHINE — a suite names an
# absolute directory on it and a run records what a process on it did — so
# committing either would be publishing a path that means nothing anywhere else
# and a verdict nobody can reproduce. The suites are meant to be re-declared over
# MCP on whatever machine the app is run on, which takes one call.
data
